{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Code landed as Gerrit change 3102, commit a6e59516654 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1). AWS is NOT changed yet: the live Lambda still lacks the role until Terraform is applied, so the daily audit still reports drift. Review advisory recorded: enrolling a break-glass role means a failed detach at the 00:00 UTC release would leave the Bedrock-invocation deny on it. Checked against infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py: _apply attaches or detaches every target, collects failures and raises PolicyApplicationError at the end, so one failing role does not strand the others; the deny covers Bedrock invocation only, and the Admin group already carries the same exposure. Remaining: operator-approved apply, then confirm live TARGET_ROLES and the next 14:00 UTC audit run."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792892257805711001,"uuid":"8525e94b-3cf4-4435-a044-52a0fc123408"}